Our flask-based framework is localized. Urls are localized too. Sometimes urls do not need to be localized.
To deal with this we created a `lurl_for` function that mimics standard `url_for` but search if there are localized urls available. If not it defaults to default language or unlocalized url.
To achieve this we use custom endpoints.

``` python
@bp.route("en/our-services", endpoint='services_en')
@bp.route("it/i-nostri-servizi", endpoint='services_it')
@login_required
def services():
  ...
